crypto-ffi: identity approval, secrets bundle import, decryption codes

What the WASM bindings already expose and Kotlin callers of
matrix-sdk-crypto-ffi cannot reach today, needed to run the same device code
on Android and on the web (Otaku, D-238):

- UserIdentity::Other.identity_needs_user_approval and
  .was_previously_verified, OlmMachine.pin_current_master_key(user_id) and
  .withdraw_verification(user_id): the pin violation of an identity that
  changed (the sender must stop until the user approves), and its approval.
- OlmMachine.import_secrets_bundle(bundle): the counterpart of
  export_secrets_bundle (restore from a backup of the secrets).
- DecryptionError::UnknownMessageIndex and
  DecryptionError::SenderIdentityNotTrusted { verification_level }: today both
  are an untyped Megolm { error } string; the caller needs to tell a key that
  may still arrive, and an unknown sender device worth a keys query, from a
  refusal.
- DecryptedEvent.sender: the sender the trust requirement checked
  (EncryptionInfo.sender).
- Device.is_deleted.

No behaviour of existing calls changes; every addition is a new method,
field or variant. Applies after 0001 and 0002, against tag
matrix-sdk-crypto-0.19.1 (commit b18166c68bb958a21f0bca8b2d8320cb53583362).
Not compiled locally (no Rust toolchain on the workstation): the build workflow
is the first compilation. To be proposed upstream (D-238).

